{0 SCE-Lang OCaml API}

SCE-Lang elaborates source programs into the explicit-environment core
calculus λE, then interprets them or compiles them to WebAssembly-GC.
This reference documents the OCaml implementation; the Lean proofs live in
the repository's [mechanization/] directory.

{1 Entry points}

Start with {!Sce.Pipeline} to compile or run source text:
{ul
 {- {!Sce.Pipeline.run} compiles, typechecks, and evaluates a whole program.}
 {- {!Sce.Pipeline.run_to_core} returns a checked core term without evaluating it.}
 {- {!Sce.Pipeline.compile_unit} compiles a file against its import interfaces.}
 {- {!Sce.Pipeline.link_artifacts} combines units in dependency order;
    {!Sce.Pipeline.run_artifact} evaluates the result.}
}

Pass a core term to {!Wasm_backend.Compile.to_binary} to produce a WasmGC
module. {!Wasm_backend.Compile.link_binary} compiles a linking term that
uses separately compiled Wasm modules.

{1 Compiler stages}

{2 Surface language}
{!Driver} parses located syntax ({!Ast}). {!Sugar} expands surface forms,
including the algebraic data types handled by {!Adt}, into named SCE terms.
{!Err} provides located diagnostics.

{2 Source calculus}
{!Sce_core.Debruijn} resolves names to environment projections.
{!Sce_core.Elab} typechecks and elaborates these terms into the core calculus.
{!Sce_core.Ast} defines the syntax; {!Sce_core.Eval} provides direct source
interpreters and {!Sce_core.Pretty} formats source types. {!Sce_core.Frames}
shares scope rules between desugaring and name resolution.

{2 Core calculus}
{!Core_lambdae.Ast} defines core terms and runtime values.
{!Core_lambdae.Check} independently checks elaborated terms;
{!Core_lambdae.Eval} evaluates them. {!Core_lambdae.Pretty} formats terms,
values, and types for diagnostics.

{2 Separate compilation and host capabilities}
{!Units.Unit} wraps a source file as a closed structure or sandboxed functor.
{!Units.Artifact} stores its interfaces and compiled term.
{!Units.Linker} checks imports and constructs core linking terms without
evaluating them. {!Units.Host} supplies printing, file reads, string operations,
and runtime loading as capability units.

{2 WebAssembly backend}
{!Wasm_backend.Compile} translates core terms into {!Wasm_backend.Ir}.
{!Wasm_backend.Abi} defines the shared value layout and indices;
{!Wasm_backend.Runtime} supplies runtime functions in that IR.
{!Wasm_backend.Emit} encodes binary modules using {!Wasm_backend.Encode}.
{!Wasm_backend.Wat} produces diagnostic text.
